FADE IN:

EXT. CITY STREET - DAY

A quiet morning. Steam curls from a coffee cart on the corner. FOOTSTEPS approach.

JORDAN
(checking a phone)
Right on time. For once.

Jordan pockets the phone and crosses the street, weaving between slow traffic.

INT. CORNER CAFE - CONTINUOUS

Warm light. The smell of fresh bread. A BARISTA glances up from the espresso machine.

BARISTA
The usual?

JORDAN
Surprise me.

The barista grins and turns to the machine. Steam hisses.

> DISSOLVE TO:

INT. OFFICE - LATER

Rows of empty desks. Jordan drops into a chair, coffee in hand, and the day begins.

FADE OUT.
